From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: diamondStar35 <ramymaherali55@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] audio: preserve live controls and gapless signal history

Keep output buffering short during ordinary playback and prepare overlap PCM
asynchronously at handoff. Reuse the running device for in-track PCM
changes independently of the gapless file-transition policy.

Separate seeks from natural gapless boundaries. Preserve compatible signal
history, re-arm EOF once, and start per-recording analysis afresh. Convert
gapless PCM before effects without reducing precision or source channels.
---
diff --git a/DOCS/interface-changes/audio-filter-history-reset.txt b/DOCS/interface-changes/audio-filter-history-reset.txt
index 4e08d89c62..761631b3d3 100644
--- a/DOCS/interface-changes/audio-filter-history-reset.txt
+++ b/DOCS/interface-changes/audio-filter-history-reset.txt
@@ -1,3 +1,6 @@
 Audio lavfi graphs with reset support retain instances and runtime options on seek.
 Compatible decoder replacements retain user audio processing. The read-only
 audio-filter-history-reset property reports support for this lifecycle.
+Natural gapless boundaries continue compatible signal history while restarting
+per-recording analysis. A stable PCM sample representation before effects
+preserves precision without forcing the first decoder's rate or channels.
